{"ts":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"13a228b577b25a0a55de1b17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.232","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-8nev0o"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A budget-truncated read is resumable on one surface and terminal on five, and the only recovery the envelope names is to abandon the budget that truncated it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Every bounded read declares two truncation mechanisms and only one of them is resumable, but the envelope reports both through the same flag pair, so a caller cannot tell a page it can continue from a page it cannot.\n\n## What is measured\n\nAt HEAD build 2026.8.14, on this 2,482-item workspace.\n\nWhen the row limit is what truncates, the envelope carries a usable continuation cursor:\n\n    pm list --status open --limit 10 --json\n      -> count 10, has_more true, truncated true,\n         next_cursor \"eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJmaW5nZXJwcmludCI6ImVjMzAy...\"\n\nWhen the token budget is what truncates, the same three flags are set and the cursor is null:\n\n    pm list --status open --limit 500 --json\n      -> count 85 of total 343, has_more true, truncated true,\n         next_cursor null,\n         output_budget_truncation.reason \"output_budget_reached\"\n         output_budget_truncation.restore_with\n           \"Re-run with --output-budget unbounded for the complete result.\"\n\nThe two cases are distinguishable only by reaching into output_budget_truncation, a key that is absent on the resumable case. Nothing in the flag pair the pagination contract is written against separates them.\n\n## The population this makes unreadable\n\nThe surface that serves the historical record is the worst case measured:\n\n    pm list-closed --limit 3000 --json\n      -> 4 rows of total 2125, has_more true, next_cursor null\n\nFour rows of 2,125 is 0.19 percent of the population, and the only recovery the envelope names is to abandon the budget:\n\n    default budget      28,073 bytes    ~7,018 tokens     4 rows\n    --output-budget unbounded  15,918,262 bytes  ~3,979,565 tokens  2125 rows\n    amplification       567x\n\nThere is no intermediate. A caller that needs row 5 must either accept a 3.98 million token response or give up. At the declared million-item scale target the ratio is not a constant, and the prescribed recovery is the exact behaviour the budget exists to prevent.\n\n## Why this is not the sibling that already shipped\n\npm-jt8aa2 closed on 2026-08-13 having shipped the disclosure block quoted above. Its third acceptance criterion reads: \"has_more true is never emitted without either a usable continuation cursor or a named alternative recovery path\". The disjunction is satisfied by restore_with, so the item is correctly closed on its own terms. This item owns the half the disjunction permitted: the named alternative is the only alternative, and it is unbounded.\n\n## The inconsistency that proves it is not a design constraint\n\nOne command already does it correctly. Under the identical reason code, pm context emits both:\n\n    pm context --limit 50 --json\n      -> has_more true,\n         output_budget_truncation.reason \"output_budget_reached\",\n         next_cursor \"eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJmaW5nZXJwcmludCI6IjllZDJm...\"\n\nMeasured across the read surfaces:\n\n    surface        budget-truncated   cursor emitted\n    list                 yes               no\n    list-open            yes               no\n    list-all             yes               no\n    list-closed          yes               no\n    next                 yes               no\n    context              yes              YES\n    search               no (limit)       YES\n\nSo a budget-truncated read can carry a continuation cursor. Five surfaces do not, and the one that does proves the capability exists in the same code path.\n\n## Collateral damage observed in this session\n\nThe defect is not confined to item listing. Reading this project's own quality gate under the default budget silently reshaped the measurement:\n\n    pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci --dry-run --json --output-budget 600\n      -> verdict \"pass\", exit_code 0, assertions array length 2\n\n    pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci --dry-run --json --output-budget unbounded\n      -> verdict \"pass\", exit_code 0, assertions array length 40\n\nThe scalar verdict was correct in both readings. The evidence set behind it was reduced by 95 percent with has_more carrying the only signal and no way to continue. A reviewer reading the budgeted form concludes the gate enforces two invariants when it enforces forty.\n\n## Why the fix belongs to the budget contract\n\nA cursor is a position in a total order. The budget truncation already knows the position at which it stopped compacting rows, because it names the compacted row paths. Emitting a cursor there is the same operation the limit path already performs. The contract question is what a continuation means when the budget rather than the caller chose the page size, and that is the declaration pm-5t33or owns, which is why this is ordered behind it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["context","output-budget","pagination","scale"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A read truncated by the output budget emits a continuation cursor that resumes the same query at the first withheld row, on every row-producing surface that emits has_more; The envelope distinguishes limit truncation from budget truncation in the pagination contract itself, so a caller reading only the declared pagination keys can tell a resumable page from a terminal one; No recovery instruction for a budget truncation names an unbounded re-read as the sole path, and the declared recovery cost is bounded by a stated multiple of the budget rather than by the corpus; A regression test walks pm list-closed to completion on a workspace larger than the default budget using only cursors, and asserts total rows delivered equals total, with peak response size bounded; The assurance verdict surface is covered by the same contract, so a gate reading its own evidence rows under a budget either receives every assertion or receives a cursor to the rest"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rxu"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":92},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-5t33or","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-j82fd3","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jt8aa2","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o87av6","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a8e2c23449252443fffb292a26f61b337f3451d4c1f43ac5c0a62310092ba3a8","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
